160
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:48,480
The answer is no,

161
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:50,480
And that comes directly from the BSA.

162
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:55,480
Specifically quote: a Scout may continue to use his existing handbook

163
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,480
as a reference and a resource.

164
00:09:57,480 --> 00:10:00,480
However, he should also have a list of the new requirements

165
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,480
for the purpose of sign-offs,

166
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:05,480
And that list is available as a PDF that you can print out.

167
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:08,480
You can put it right in the handbook from the BSA

168
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:13,480
And I will have a link to that in the podcast notes too.

169
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,480
And so Scouts don't have to run out and get a new handbook.

170
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,480
You don't have to wait for the new handbook

171
00:10:18,480 --> 00:10:20,480
to apply the new requirements.

172
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:22,480
And I'll say the last little bit of information here is-

